{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "4c8ddf4f-0ad3-4518-8dfe-6b7da581f69d",
    "name": "E-Health Care API",
    "description": "E-Health Care — Complete Postman Collection v2.1\n\nGenerated from Spring Boot source code analysis.\n\nArchitecture:\n- Backend: Spring Boot on port 8080\n- Authentication: JWT Bearer Token (3 separate tokens per role)\n- Tokens: sent via Authorization: Bearer <token> header\n- Cookies: also set by server (jwt-admin-token, jwt-doctor-token, jwt-patient-token)\n\nSetup:\n1. Import EHC_Environment.json into Postman Environments\n2. Set base_url = http://localhost:8080\n3. Run Login requests — tokens are auto-saved via test scripts\n4. All protected requests reference {{admin_token}}, {{doctor_token}}, {{patient_token}}\n\nFolders:\n- Admin Auth        : /admin/api/auth\n- Admin Management  : /api/admin\n- Admin Patient CRUD: /admin/api/patients\n- Doctor            : /api/doctor\n- Patient           : /api/patient\n- Patient Appointment: /api/patient/appointment\n- Public            : /api",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json",
    "_exporter_id": "52299616",
    "_collection_link": "https://go.postman.co/collection/52299616-4c8ddf4f-0ad3-4518-8dfe-6b7da581f69d?source=collection_link"
  },
